{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Speech Recognition (ASR) \u2014 CTC, RNN-T, Attention Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: greedy CTC decode"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ctc_greedy(frame_logits, blank=0, vocab=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # frame_logits: list of per-frame probability vectors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preds = [max(range(len(p)), key=lambda i: p[i]) for p in frame_logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prev = -1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in preds:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if p != prev and p != blank:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out.append(p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prev = p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \"\".join(vocab[i] for i in out) if vocab else out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two rules: collapse consecutive repeats, drop blanks. Example: `a a _ _ a b b _ c` \u2192 `a a b c`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: beam-search CTC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ctc_beam(frame_logits, beam=8, blank=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    beams = [([], 0.0)]  # (tokens, log_prob)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in frame_logits:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        log_p = [math.log(max(pi, 1e-10)) for pi in p]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        candidates = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for seq, lp in beams:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for t, lpt in enumerate(log_p):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                new = seq[:] if t == blank else (seq + [t] if not seq or seq[-1] != t else seq)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                candidates.append((new, lp + lpt))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        candidates.sort(key=lambda x: -x[1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        beams = candidates[:beam]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return beams[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Production uses prefix tree beam search with LM fusion; this is the conceptual skeleton."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: WER"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def wer(ref, hyp):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r, h = ref.split(), hyp.split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dp = [[0] * (len(h) + 1) for _ in range(len(r) + 1)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(len(r) + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dp[i][0] = i"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for j in range(len(h) + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dp[0][j] = j"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(1, len(r) + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(1, len(h) + 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            cost = 0 if r[i - 1] == h[j - 1] else 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            dp[i][j] = min("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dp[len(r)][len(h)] / max(1, len(r))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: inference against Whisper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import whisper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = whisper.load_model(\"large-v3-turbo\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = model.transcribe(\"clip.wav\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(result[\"text\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One-liner for the strongest general ASR in 2026. Runs on a 24 GB GPU at ~20\u00d7 realtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: streaming with Parakeet or wav2vec 2.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "asr = pipeline(\"automatic-speech-recognition\", model=\"nvidia/parakeet-tdt-1.1b\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for chunk in streaming_audio():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(asr(chunk, return_timestamps=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Streaming ASR needs chunked encoder attention and carryover state; use a library that supports it (NeMo for Parakeet, `transformers` pipeline with `chunk_length_s`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. It greedily decodes a hand-crafted CTC output and computes WER against a reference.\n2. **Medium.** Implement the prefix-tree beam search in Step 2 properly (account for the blank merge rule). Compare with greedy on a 10-example synthetic dataset.\n3. **Hard.** Use `whisper-large-v3-turbo` on [LibriSpeech test-clean](https://www.openslr.org/12). Compute WER on the first 100 utterances. Compare with published numbers."
      ]
    }
